Architecture

Browser (index.html)
   │  POST /api/generate {prompt, genre, style, panels}
   ▼
FastAPI backend
   ├─ 1. Gemini text model → JSON script (title + panels)
   ├─ 2. Gemini image model → one image per panel (run in parallel)
   └─ 3. Return {title, panels:[{caption, dialogue, image}]}
   ▼
Browser renders comic grid

API design

POST /api/generate accepts the request body above and returns the story JSON
Errors return { "detail": "..." } with an HTTP error code (the frontend already reads detail)
/docs is the auto-generated FastAPI documentation, already linked in the navbar

UI/UX design

Comic-book theme: halftone dots, bold outlines, offset shadows
Fonts: Bowlby One for headings, Atkinson Hyperlegible for body text
Palette: cyan, magenta and yellow on a paper background
Layout: sticky form on the left, comic page on the right, collapsing to one column on small screens
The first panel spans the full width as an "establishing shot"

Design decisions

Prompt the text model to return strict JSON so the backend can parse it reliably
Reuse one shared character and style description in every image prompt to keep panels consistent
Images returned as base64 or URLs (the frontend accepts both)
